  "note": "Ishita Banerjee, 34, works as a diagnostic-clinic records assistant off the lane and lives exclusively in tall-flats upper A. Every day she sleeps 22:30-06:00, cooks breakfast 06:00-06:30, eats until 06:45 and gets ready. Monday-Saturday she leaves at 07:00 for work 07:30-15:00, with lunch 12:00-12:30. She returns at 15:30, rests and is awake at home from 16:00-19:30. Sunday she stays home, reads, cooks lunch 11:30-12:00 and rests. Every evening she cooks 19:30-20:00, eats until 20:30 and reads until sleep. Upper A is private with no posted visiting window: admission still requires a present, nonsleeping host. Home deliberately remains the exact door location. The alias anchor.ishita.tall_flats_front follows Nirmal/Sahana's front-threshold convention. The 1680 cm upper-home-to-front route is a conservative provisional stair/landing allowance, not measured geometry; R5-02 must derive its navigable polyline from the built stair and side entrance. The remaining 2520 cm is an authored off-lane clinic leg. Travel is ceil(total length/140): 12 + 18 = 30 minutes each way. All unordered zone pairs have one explicitly authored canonical travel row.",
